title: $:/plugins/btheado/notebook-kit/readme

This plugin provides a `<$notebook-kit/>` widget that renders TiddlyWiki
tiddlers as cells in an [[Observable Notebook Kit|https://observablehq.com/notebook-kit/]]
notebook.

To create a new notebook, add the following transclusion to a tiddler:

```
{{||$:/plugins/btheado/notebook-kit/NotebookStoryTemplate}}
```

This template wraps the `<$notebook-kit/>` widget with a story river, allowing
the notebook's cells to be edited in place while viewing the notebook.

The content of the `<$notebook-kit/>` widget completely determines the
notebook's layout. After the widget has rendered, it scans the generated DOM
for elements that identify notebook cells. Each matching element specifies the
tiddler that should be evaluated as a notebook cell.

An element with the `tc-notebook-output` class is treated as a notebook cell.
The title of the cell tiddler is taken from its `data-tiddler-title` attribute.

For example:

```wiki
<$notebook-kit>
<div class="tc-notebook-output" data-tiddler-title="mynotebook/cell1"/>
<div class="tc-notebook-output" data-tiddler-title="mynotebook/cell2"/>
</$notebook-kit>
```

In this example, the cell tiddlers are displayed as notebook output but cannot
be edited from within the notebook. They are still evaluated and rendered as
notebook cells.

